# Merkle claim artifacts — generated, NEVER committed.
#
# `apps/web/public/` is served statically, so a committed proofs.json would be
# published at /claim-data/proofs.json and read as the AUTHORITATIVE claim
# table. Everything generated there so far is dry-run/fixture data, and
# shipping a fixture as the real allocation is the exact failure this rule
# exists to prevent. The root-level dir holds the same run's tree/root/summary
# — same reasoning, it just isn't web-served.
#
# Publishing the real table must be a conscious `git add -f`, never a side
# effect of `git add -A`.
/claim-data/
apps/web/public/claim-data/
